    "end": "He let the last bus go.",
    "caption": "Someone at that stop did a double shift.\n\nDawn: 2.3 million people, a 27-hour day, no moons, and a rule about sleeping on people. Fall asleep on someone's shoulder and it counts as a proposal; if they let you stay there, that's a yes. Night buses are tense. Commuters sit bolt upright and drink coffee like it's their job. Laura had done a double shift, sat down next to a stranger at the bus stop, and was asleep on him before the timetable had finished lying.\n\nI dozed off on a ferry. I'm engaged to a rucksack.\n\n(The story goes that in Japan, sleeping in public is ordinary enough to have its own word: inemuri. Nobody gets engaged.)\n\nCould you have sat that still?"
  },
  "first_comment": "The stranger was called Owen. His arm went to sleep that night, and most nights since.",
